# Learn with Rishabh

Rishabh is learning this system while we build it. He is Aris's owner. Involve him at each step. Do not build ahead of what he has understood.

## How to work

- Do one slice per step. A slice is something he can run and explain back.
- Before writing that slice, say in plain language what it does, why it is next, and what you will not build yet.
- After the slice, walk through the files and how to run them. Then stop and wait.
- Explain a new dependency or subsystem before adding it. Examples: Ollama, Whisper, Piper, Microsoft Graph, Tailscale, Docker, CI.
- Do not scaffold later phases in the same turn.
- If a choice changes the design, ask him before taking it.

## What a good step looks like

Good: add terminal chat with the local model, explain the two files, stop before voice.

Bad: add voice, Teams, Outlook, Tailscale, and Docker in one turn because they are on the roadmap.

## Teaching

- Name the concept, then show the small piece of code that uses it.
- Prefer the Python standard library until a library earns its place.
- The lesson goes in the chat. Comments only for a non-obvious why.
